SUMMARY:Serendipity Brunch
LOCATION:Lunasol
DESCRIPTION:Category: Food & Beverage\, Member Mixer\nPrice: $65.00 per per
 son\nAvailability: 8 spots left\nStatus: Available\nEvent URL: https://mem
 bers.thequinhouse.com/events/208334\n\nMake your Saturday a little more se
 rendipitous with a leisurely brunch hosted by The ‘Quin’s Membership T
 eam. Gather in Lunasol for an afternoon centered around good food\, easy c
 onversation\, and the opportunity to connect with fellow members\, whether
  meeting for the first time or discovering a familiar face in a new way.\n
 \nSettle in over a seasonal selection of chef-crafted entrées\, accompani
 ed by family-style favorites and classic brunch cocktails\, including mimo
 sas and Bloody Marys. With a relaxed setting and plenty of time to linger 
 around the table\, it’s an afternoon made for conversation\, connection\
 , and seeing where a little serendipity might lead.\n\nSpend your Saturday
  at The ‘House unhurried\, social\, and best enjoyed in good company.\n\
 n*Tickets are $65 per person\, plus tax\, and are reserved for members onl
 y. Cancellations within 72 hours of the event\, or failure to attend\, wil
 l be charged in full. Please inform us of any dietary needs or restriction
 s by emailing happening@thequin.com at least 72 hours prior to the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/208334
CATEGORIES:Food & Beverage,Member Mixer
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-210562@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261116T180000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261116T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261116T193000
SUMMARY:Author Talk: "The Greatest Adventurer" with Geoffrey Kent and Ben M
 ezrich 
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nStatus: You are Confirmed\nEve
 nt URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/210562\n\n6:00PM Reception
 \, 6:30PM Discussion \nFrom a single Land Rover in the African bush to th
 e global travel company Abercrombie & Kent\, Geoffrey Kent has built a lif
 e around taking the road less traveled. Join The ’Quin for a conversatio
 n with the explorer and entrepreneur\, moderated by co-author of The Grea
 test Adventurer\, Ben Mezrich\, on the adventures\, ambitions\, and person
 al stakes behind an extraordinary career.\n\nDrawing on his memoir\, The 
 Greatest Adventurer: From the Wilds of Africa to a Billion-Dollar Travel E
 mpire\, Kent will share stories from a lifetime of exploration—from cros
 sing Africa alone by motorbike at sixteen to navigating the Amazon and pio
 neering a new era of luxury travel. Guided by the philosophy “Shoot with
  a camera\, not with a gun\,” his work has helped shape the relationship
  between travel and conservation.\n\nBeyond the expeditions lies an equall
 y compelling story of entrepreneurship and family: the risks of building a
  global business\, the relationships tested along the way\, and the compli
 cated question of what we leave behind. Together\, Kent and Mezrich will e
 xplore the instinct to venture further—and what it takes to know when yo
 u have arrived.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members o
 nly. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served. Cancellati
 ons made within 24 hours of the event\, or failure to attend\, will result
  in a $25 charge.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/210562
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
