BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-209702@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261117T130000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261117T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261117T150000
SUMMARY:90 Minutes of Innovation
LOCATION:The Pub
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 28 spots lef
 t\nStatus: You are Confirmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/
 events/209702\n\n1:00PM Program\, 2:30PM Networking\nWhat happens when art
 ificial intelligence steps off the screen and into the physical world? Joi
 n The ’Quin for an afternoon exploring how robotics is changing the way 
 we move\, work\, and interact with technology - and what it takes to bring
  those advances into everyday life.\n\nJohn Werner - venture capitalist\, 
 active member of the MIT community\, and Forbes AI columnist - will lead a
  conversation with Conor Walsh\, Harvard’s Paul A. Maeder Professor of E
 ngineering and Applied Sciences and founder of the Harvard Biodesign Lab\,
  and Tom Ryden\, Executive Director of MassRobotics.\n\nWalsh’s work in 
 soft robotics and wearable exosuits is helping people regain mobility and 
 perform physically demanding tasks with less strain. At MassRobotics\, Ryd
 en connects entrepreneurs\, researchers\, investors\, and industry to help
  emerging robotics companies grow. Together\, they offer complementary per
 spectives on the journey from a promising prototype to a technology that i
 mproves people’s lives.\n\nThe evening will also mark five years of inno
 vation programming at The ’Quin\, with Werner sharing highlights from mo
 re than 50 programs that have brought members into conversation with the p
 eople shaping our future. From the inaugural TEDxBoston in 2021 to today�
 �s explorations of robotics and physical AI\, curiosity remains at the hea
 rt of it all.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members onl
 y. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served. Cancellation
 s made within 24 hours of the event\, or failure to attend\, will result i
 n a $25 charge.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/209702
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
