DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Impact Fund\, The 'Quin Impact Fund\nPrice: F
 ree\nAvailability: 20 spots left\nStatus: futureSale\nEvent URL: https://m
 embers.thequinhouse.com/events/211080\n\nJoin fellow members for a meaning
 ful evening of service at Pine Street Inn’s Men’s Inn shelter\, helpin
 g serve dinner to guests in a welcoming\, restaurant-style setting. Throug
 h a shared meal and thoughtful hospitality\, volunteers help create an atm
 osphere where every guest feels welcomed\, respected\, and cared for.\n\nT
 his hands-on opportunity supports Pine Street Inn’s mission of helping i
 ndividuals move from homelessness to stable housing. Come together to give
  your time\, connect with the broader Boston community\, and contribute to
  an evening centered on dignity\, kindness\, and the comfort of a warm mea
 l.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only. To ensur
 e a smooth and comfortable volunteer experience\, we ask that attire be bo
 th respectful and practical- long pants and closed-toe shoes are required.
  All volunteers will need to wear a hat or hairnet\; you are welcome to br
 ing your own baseball cap\, or a hairnet will be provided. Volunteers with
  facial hair will be required to wear a beardnet to maintain a safe and po
 lished service environment.
