BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-211944@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261207T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261207T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261207T190000
SUMMARY:Author Talk: "Unspeakable" with Christina Wing
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 100 spots left\n
 Status: futureSale\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/211
 944\n\n5:00PM Reception\, 5:30PM Discussion\n\nSome of the most important 
 conversations are the ones we hesitate to have. Join Harvard Business Scho
 ol faculty member\, Wingspan Legacy Partners founder\, and author Christin
 a Wing for a thoughtful conversation with The ’Quin House Co-Founder San
 dy Edgerley\, exploring Wing’s latest book\, Unspeakable: The Taboo Topi
 cs We Avoid and How to Talk About Them. From money and succession to failu
 re\, retirement\, and family dynamics\, Wing examines why certain subjects
  feel off-limits\, and how avoiding them can quietly undermine trust\, rel
 ationships\, and the decisions that shape our lives.\n\nDrawing on decades
  of experience across classrooms\, boardrooms\, and family enterprises\, W
 ing will share stories and practical tools for approaching sensitive conve
 rsations with clarity\, compassion\, and respect. In dialogue with Sandy E
 dgerley\, she will explore what becomes possible when we move beyond small
  talk\, offering members fresh perspectives on navigating difficult discus
 sions and building stronger\, more honest connections at work and at home.
 \n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Compliment
 ary light bites and refreshments will be served. Cancellations made within
  24 hours of the event\, or failure to attend\, will result in a $25 charg
 e.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/211944
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
