BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-211943@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261208T173000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261208T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261208T190000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat & Screening: "MANGOK" 
LOCATION:The Muse
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 60 spots lef
 t\nStatus: futureSale\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/
 211943\n\n5:30PM Reception\, 6:00PM Screening\, 6:25PM Discussion\nTwo day
 s before World Human Rights Day\, join us for a moving ’Quin Chat with M
 angok Bol\, filmmaker Joshua Bennett\, and RefugePoint founder Sasha Chano
 ff\, exploring the extraordinary story behind Bennett’s documentary\, MA
 NGOK. A South Sudanese “Lost Boy” who made Boston his home\, Mangok sp
 ent more than a decade searching for family members separated by war. Afte
 r learning that his brother and sister-in-law had been killed and their fo
 ur children were missing\, he embarked on a determined search with the sup
 port of Chanoff and RefugePoint. Three of his nieces and nephews have sinc
 e been welcomed to Boston\, while the search for the fourth continues in S
 outh Sudan.\n\nThrough a conversation about perseverance\, family reunific
 ation\, and the profound impact of community\, our guests will reflect on 
 the personal journey at the heart of the film and the broader challenges f
 acing displaced families around the world. Together\, we will explore what
  it means to rebuild a life\, the bonds that endure across borders\, and h
 ow one person’s refusal to give up can inspire a community to open its d
 oors and its heart.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for membe
 rs only. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served. Cancel
 lations made within 24 hours of the event\, or failure to attend\, will re
 sult in a $25 charge.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/211943
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
